elif page == "ℹ️  About":
    st.markdown("<h1 style='color:#e2e8f0;'>ℹ️ About This System</h1>", unsafe_allow_html=True)

    # CKD Overview
    st.markdown("<div class='section-header'>🫁 What is Chronic Kidney Disease?</div>", unsafe_allow_html=True)
    st.markdown("""
<div style='background:#1e2535; border-radius:12px; padding:24px; border:1px solid #2d3748; color:#cbd5e0; line-height:1.8;'>

**Chronic Kidney Disease (CKD)** is a long-term condition where the kidneys gradually lose their
filtering ability over months or years. The kidneys play a critical role in removing waste products
and excess fluid from the blood, regulating blood pressure, and maintaining electrolyte balance.

CKD is classified into five stages based on **eGFR (estimated Glomerular Filtration Rate)**:

| Stage | eGFR Range        | Description                  |
|-------|-------------------|------------------------------|
| 1–2   | ≥ 60 mL/min       | Mild – kidney damage present |
| 3     | 30–59 mL/min      | Moderate reduction           |
| 4     | 15–29 mL/min      | Severe reduction             |
| 5     | < 15 mL/min       | Kidney failure               |

**Risk factors** include diabetes, hypertension, family history, obesity, and smoking.
Early detection and management can significantly slow disease progression.
</div>
""", unsafe_allow_html=True)

    st.markdown("<br>", unsafe_allow_html=True)

    # Prediction Workflow
    st.markdown("<div class='section-header'>⚙️ Prediction Workflow</div>", unsafe_allow_html=True)
    workflow_steps = [
        ("📥", "Data Collection",
         "The user inputs 35 clinical biomarkers covering demographics, kidney function markers, "
         "electrolytes, blood panel, glucose & lipids, serum proteins, and risk factors."),
        ("🔄", "Data Preprocessing",
         "Binary categorical variables (Diabetes, Hypertension, etc.) are encoded. "
         "All numerical features are standardised using StandardScaler fitted on training data."),
        ("🤖", "Model Inference",
         "The preprocessed feature vector is passed to the best-performing trained ML classifier. "
         "Predicted class index is decoded back to a human-readable stage label."),
        ("📊", "Confidence Estimation",
         "Where available (for Logistic Regression and Random Forest), class probabilities are "
         "computed using predict_proba(), giving a confidence score for each stage."),
        ("💊", "Clinical Recommendation",
         "Based on the predicted stage, tailored clinical advice is displayed to guide "
         "the patient or clinician on next steps."),
    ]
    for icon, title, desc in workflow_steps:
        st.markdown(f"""
        <div style='display:flex; gap:16px; padding:16px; background:#1e2535;
                    border-radius:12px; margin-bottom:10px; border:1px solid #2d3748;'>
            <div style='font-size:1.8rem; flex-shrink:0;'>{icon}</div>
            <div>
                <div style='color:#e2e8f0; font-weight:600; font-size:1rem; margin-bottom:4px;'>{title}</div>
                <div style='color:#a0aec0; font-size:0.875rem; line-height:1.6;'>{desc}</div>
            </div>
        </div>""", unsafe_allow_html=True)

    st.markdown("<br>", unsafe_allow_html=True)

    # ML Algorithms
    st.markdown("<div class='section-header'>🤖 Machine Learning Algorithms</div>", unsafe_allow_html=True)
    algos = [
        ("Logistic Regression", "A linear probabilistic classifier that models the relationship "
         "between features and class probabilities using the softmax function. "
         "Serves as the interpretable baseline model."),
        ("Decision Tree", "A non-linear tree-structured classifier that recursively splits "
         "the feature space. Highly interpretable but prone to overfitting without pruning."),
        ("Random Forest ⭐", "An ensemble of decision trees trained on bootstrapped subsets "
         "(bagging). Reduces variance through averaging, handles non-linearity and feature "
         "interactions well. Typically our best performer."),
        ("Gradient Boosting", "An ensemble method that builds trees sequentially, each correcting "
         "the errors of the previous. Achieves high accuracy but trains slower than Random Forest."),
    ]
    for name, desc in algos:
        st.markdown(f"""
        <div style='padding:14px 18px; background:#1e2535; border-radius:10px;
                    margin-bottom:8px; border-left:3px solid #3182ce;'>
            <div style='color:#63b3ed; font-weight:600; margin-bottom:4px;'>{name}</div>
            <div style='color:#a0aec0; font-size:0.85rem; line-height:1.6;'>{desc}</div>
        </div>""", unsafe_allow_html=True)

    st.markdown("<br>", unsafe_allow_html=True)

    # Disclaimer
